    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d286-a1">

                <pb facs="0551" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg531"/>

                <head>Mr. Cunard to Mr.
                        Archibald.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 20, 1864</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I wrote to you on the 8th instant
                    respecting the restrictions imposed by the collector of customs on shipments to
                    Nassau. The royal mail steamship Corsica is advertised to sail on the 29th
                    instant, and I have applications from merchants to send freight by her, but on
                    application at the custom-house I am informed that, before the ship clears, I
                    shall have to give the bond and securities, as stated to you in my letter. As I
                    cannot give these, the steamer must proceed to Nassau without freight; and
                    should it prove that this restriction is not consistent with the treaty
                    stipulations between the United States and Great Britain, I have to request that
                    you will submit, for the consideration of Lord Lyons, that I have a claim for
                    the loss sustained thereby.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c., &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. CUNARDM.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. M. Archibald</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Her Britannic Majesty’s Consul.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
